  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-automations-e4-7f31c2ad",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 6300,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 542.5,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (automations run lifecycle, slice E4): the automations domain becomes a CAPABILITY\nsurface. routes/automations.ts swaps r.use(requireAuth) for E1's requireUserOrApiKey, so every route\nunder it admits a platform JWT (byte-identical delegation) OR an ekoa_gk_ gateway key, and the shared/\ndescriptors carry auth:'user-or-key'. TWO DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS: the run SSE stream stays token-query\n(its ?token= is a real jti-bearing platform JWT - a key must never ride a session token that outlives\nits own revocation, E1 review), and create's class names the CREDENTIAL, not the role: org-admin\ncreation authority is still enforced in service.canCreateAutomation against the role the middleware\nre-reads LIVE from the users store on every key call.\nNEW ROUTE: GET /api/v1/automations/runs/:id/logs -> service.getRunLogs -> persistence.runLogsFromSteps,\nowner-scoped by the SAME canSeeRun predicate as GET /runs/:id (identical uniform 404, so logs can never\nbecome an existence oracle the run endpoint is not).\nLOG CAPTURE MOVES INTO THE ENGINE. Step stdout/stderr used to exist ONLY as ephemeral SSE\nstep_output_chunk frames, so a key-driven caller with no stream could never read it. engine.runOrRehearse\nnow ALWAYS passes an emitOutputChunk (previously only when an SSE emitter existed) into a per-run\npersistence.createStepLogAccumulator, and attaches the bounded tail to each StepRecord as the step\nfinishes - so every persist site (the per-step update AND every finalize exit, including cancelled and\nfailed) carries it. The SSE forward is unchanged when an emitter is bound; nothing new reaches the wire\nrun shape (toWireStep / automationStepEventPayload build explicit fields).\nIDEMPOTENT CREATE: POST /:id/runs takes idempotencyKey (body) or the Idempotency-Key header - one field,\nand a DISAGREEMENT between the two is refused (VALIDATION_FAILED), never resolved. service.startRun\nINSERTS the dedupe mapping BEFORE creating the run (data/stores automation_run_idempotency), so the\nduplicate-_id refusal settles a concurrent race; the loser reads the winner's runId and answers 200\n(fresh create stays 202). The claim loop NEVER falls through unclaimed - an unrecorded run would let the\nnext retry start a second one - so an unresolvable claim fails closed (IDEMPOTENCY_UNRESOLVED -> 500,\nthe same key safe to retry). A key-admitted create writes ONE activity row {keyId, xClient, automationId,\nrunId, idempotent} through the single audit path - x-client is TRACE ONLY (contract rule 3).\n/logs RECONCILES ITS TWO SOURCES (review finding 1): the streamed tail and the AUTHORITATIVE output.stdout\nare NOT copies (the daemon's progress channel is one undiscriminated chunk), so the longer one is served and\n`truncated` is set when the other carried text it does not contain - never a 200 KB capture answered as a\none-line log claiming completeness. x-client is length-capped in E1's middleware (X_CLIENT_MAX) so every\nconsumer inherits the bound before it reaches an audit row.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (automations run lifecycle, slice E4): the automations domain becomes a CAPABILITY\nsurface. routes/automations.ts swaps r.use(requireAuth) for E1's requireUserOrApiKey, so every route\nunder it admits a platform JWT (byte-identical delegation) OR an ekoa_gk_ gateway key, and the shared/\ndescriptors carry auth:'user-or-key'. TWO DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS: the run SSE stream stays token-query\n(its ?token= is a real jti-bearing platform JWT - a key must never ride a session token that outlives\nits own revocation, E1 review), and create's class names the CREDENTIAL, not the role: org-admin\ncreation authority is still enforced in service.canCreateAutomation against the role the middleware\nre-reads LIVE from the users store on every key call.\nNEW ROUTE: GET /api/v1/automations/runs/:id/logs -> service.getRunLogs -> persistence.runLogsFromSteps,\nowner-scoped by the SAME canSeeRun predicate as GET /runs/:id (identical uniform 404, so logs can never\nbecome an existence oracle the run endpoint is not).\nLOG CAPTURE MOVES INTO THE ENGINE. Step stdout/stderr used to exist ONLY as ephemeral SSE\nstep_output_chunk frames, so a key-driven caller with no stream could never read it. engine.runOrRehearse\nnow ALWAYS passes an emitOutputChunk (previously only when an SSE emitter existed) into a per-run\npersistence.createStepLogAccumulator, and attaches the bounded tail to each StepRecord as the step\nfinishes - so every persist site (the per-step update AND every finalize exit, including cancelled and\nfailed) carries it. The SSE forward is unchanged when an emitter is bound; nothing new reaches the wire\nrun shape (toWireStep / automationStepEventPayload build explicit fields).\nIDEMPOTENT CREATE: POST /:id/runs takes idempotencyKey (body) or the Idempotency-Key header - one field,\nand a DISAGREEMENT between the two is refused (VALIDATION_FAILED), never resolved. service.startRun\nINSERTS the dedupe mapping BEFORE creating the run (data/stores automation_run_idempotency), so the\nduplicate-_id refusal settles a concurrent race; the loser reads the winner's runId and answers 200\n(fresh create stays 202). The claim loop NEVER falls through unclaimed - an unrecorded run would let the\nnext retry start a second one - so an unresolvable claim fails closed (IDEMPOTENCY_UNRESOLVED -> 500,\nthe same key safe to retry). A key-admitted create writes ONE activity row {keyId, xClient, automationId,\nrunId, idempotent} through the single audit path - x-client is TRACE ONLY (contract rule 3).\n/logs RECONCILES ITS TWO SOURCES (review finding 1): the streamed tail and the AUTHORITATIVE output.stdout\nare NOT copies (the daemon's progress channel is one undiscriminated chunk), so the longer one is served and\n`truncated` is set when the other carried text it does not contain - never a 200 KB capture answered as a\none-line log claiming completeness. x-client is length-capped in E1's middleware (X_CLIENT_MAX) so every\nconsumer inherits the bound before it reaches an audit row.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (automations run lifecycle, slice E4): the automations domain becomes a CAPABILITY\nsurface. routes/automations.ts swaps r.use(requireAuth) for E1's requireUserOrApiKey, so every route\nunder it admits a platform JWT (byte-identical delegation) OR an ekoa_gk_ gateway key, and the shared/\ndescriptors carry auth:'user-or-key'. TWO DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS: the run SSE stream stays token-query\n(its ?token= is a real jti-bearing platform JWT - a key must never ride a session token that outlives\nits own revocation, E1 review), and create's class names the CREDENTIAL, not the role: org-admin\ncreation authority is still enforced in service.canCreateAutomation against the role the middleware\nre-reads LIVE from the users store on every key call.\nNEW ROUTE: GET /api/v1/automations/runs/:id/logs -> service.getRunLogs -> persistence.runLogsFromSteps,\nowner-scoped by the SAME canSeeRun predicate as GET /runs/:id (identical uniform 404, so logs can never\nbecome an existence oracle the run endpoint is not).\nLOG CAPTURE MOVES INTO THE ENGINE. Step stdout/stderr used to exist ONLY as ephemeral SSE\nstep_output_chunk frames, so a key-driven caller with no stream could never read it. engine.runOrRehearse\nnow ALWAYS passes an emitOutputChunk (previously only when an SSE emitter existed) into a per-run\npersistence.createStepLogAccumulator, and attaches the bounded tail to each StepRecord as the step\nfinishes - so every persist site (the per-step update AND every finalize exit, including cancelled and\nfailed) carries it. The SSE forward is unchanged when an emitter is bound; nothing new reaches the wire\nrun shape (toWireStep / automationStepEventPayload build explicit fields).\nIDEMPOTENT CREATE: POST /:id/runs takes idempotencyKey (body) or the Idempotency-Key header - one field,\nand a DISAGREEMENT between the two is refused (VALIDATION_FAILED), never resolved. service.startRun\nINSERTS the dedupe mapping BEFORE creating the run (data/stores automation_run_idempotency), so the\nduplicate-_id refusal settles a concurrent race; the loser reads the winner's runId and answers 200\n(fresh create stays 202). The claim loop NEVER falls through unclaimed - an unrecorded run would let the\nnext retry start a second one - so an unresolvable claim fails closed (IDEMPOTENCY_UNRESOLVED -> 500,\nthe same key safe to retry). A key-admitted create writes ONE activity row {keyId, xClient, automationId,\nrunId, idempotent} through the single audit path - x-client is TRACE ONLY (contract rule 3).\n/logs RECONCILES ITS TWO SOURCES (review finding 1): the streamed tail and the AUTHORITATIVE output.stdout\nare NOT copies (the daemon's progress channel is one undiscriminated chunk), so the longer one is served and\n`truncated` is set when the other carried text it does not contain - never a 200 KB capture answered as a\none-line log claiming completeness. x-client is length-capped in E1's middleware (X_CLIENT_MAX) so every\nconsumer inherits the bound before it reaches an audit row.",
