  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-knowledge-e5-5d0a7c62",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 6890,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 507.5,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (knowledge search/read over REST, slice E5): the knowledge domain gains a CAPABILITY\nREAD surface. NOTHING moves in knowledge/ itself - the org-partitioned vault + FTS5 index are unchanged,\nand the in-process agent path (server.ts setKnowledgeToolSearch/setKnowledgeToolRead -> agents/) is\nuntouched. What changes is REACH: routes/knowledge.ts now has TWO admission tiers in ONE router.\nTIER 1 (mounted BEFORE the router-wide requireAuth, so express's middleware order is what separates the\ntiers - the same shape automations.ts uses for its SSE route): GET /collections, GET /documents,\nNEW POST /search, NEW GET /documents/:collection/:docId, all requireUserOrApiKey / auth:'user-or-key'.\nTIER 2 (after r.use(requireAuth)): ingest, delete, sources, uploads, reindex, index-status - platform\nsession ONLY. This slice opens NO ingestion surface to a key; requireAuth refuses an ekoa_gk_ bearer as an\nunparseable JWT, which the contract suite pins on all eight write/admin routes.\nTHE TWO NEW ROUTES REUSE, THEY DO NOT REIMPLEMENT: service.searchDocuments wraps index-store.search - the\nSAME function the agent tool seam calls, org partitioning in its signature - and service.readDocument wraps\nreadDocWithShared (own vault shadows the shared corpus). A `collection` filter narrows AFTER the FTS query\n(the index has no collection predicate and gaining one would change the shape agents/ depends on), so a\nfiltered search over-fetches and is a relevance-ordered narrowing, stated in-code, not a WHERE scan.\nORG SCOPE IS STRUCTURAL: it rides actorOf(req)/the audited ActivityActor and nothing else. No knowledge\nschema declares an org/tenant field, zod strips unknown keys, and a grep gate in the new scoping suite\nbans reading an org out of req.body/query/params/headers anywhere in knowledge/ or routes/knowledge.ts.\nPATH SHAPE: a collection and a docId are each ONE vault segment (shared/ KnowledgeSegment mirrors paths.ts\nSEGMENT_RE, '.'/'..' refused), so '/' is unrepresentable and two ordinary express :params suffice - no\nwildcard and no ?permalink= workaround as memvault's multi-segment permalinks needed.\n`_shared` TIGHTENS: assertNotSharedActor was 'cannot MUTATE the corpus'; it is now 'is never a request\nactor at all' - search, read AND the two browse routes refuse a caller presenting the shared org id (403,\nuniform message). Nothing is lost: every org still searches and reads the corpus, and each hit/document\nsays scope:'org'|'shared' while the underlying orgId never reaches the wire.\nAUDIT: the two NEW routes write ONE activity row + ONE structured console line per call through the single\naudit path (category 'knowledge', verdict ok|denied|not_found|forbidden|error, keyId+xClient on a key\ncall), refusals included. The query TEXT and the document body are deliberately NOT recorded - a search\nstring here is a client's confidential matter; the row carries the call's shape, not its content.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (knowledge search/read over REST, slice E5): the knowledge domain gains a CAPABILITY\nREAD surface. NOTHING moves in knowledge/ itself - the org-partitioned vault + FTS5 index are unchanged,\nand the in-process agent path (server.ts setKnowledgeToolSearch/setKnowledgeToolRead -> agents/) is\nuntouched. What changes is REACH: routes/knowledge.ts now has TWO admission tiers in ONE router.\nTIER 1 (mounted BEFORE the router-wide requireAuth, so express's middleware order is what separates the\ntiers - the same shape automations.ts uses for its SSE route): GET /collections, GET /documents,\nNEW POST /search, NEW GET /documents/:collection/:docId, all requireUserOrApiKey / auth:'user-or-key'.\nTIER 2 (after r.use(requireAuth)): ingest, delete, sources, uploads, reindex, index-status - platform\nsession ONLY. This slice opens NO ingestion surface to a key; requireAuth refuses an ekoa_gk_ bearer as an\nunparseable JWT, which the contract suite pins on all eight write/admin routes.\nTHE TWO NEW ROUTES REUSE, THEY DO NOT REIMPLEMENT: service.searchDocuments wraps index-store.search - the\nSAME function the agent tool seam calls, org partitioning in its signature - and service.readDocument wraps\nreadDocWithShared (own vault shadows the shared corpus). A `collection` filter narrows AFTER the FTS query\n(the index has no collection predicate and gaining one would change the shape agents/ depends on), so a\nfiltered search over-fetches and is a relevance-ordered narrowing, stated in-code, not a WHERE scan.\nORG SCOPE IS STRUCTURAL: it rides actorOf(req)/the audited ActivityActor and nothing else. No knowledge\nschema declares an org/tenant field, zod strips unknown keys, and a grep gate in the new scoping suite\nbans reading an org out of req.body/query/params/headers anywhere in knowledge/ or routes/knowledge.ts.\nPATH SHAPE: a collection and a docId are each ONE vault segment (shared/ KnowledgeSegment mirrors paths.ts\nSEGMENT_RE, '.'/'..' refused), so '/' is unrepresentable and two ordinary express :params suffice - no\nwildcard and no ?permalink= workaround as memvault's multi-segment permalinks needed.\n`_shared` TIGHTENS: assertNotSharedActor was 'cannot MUTATE the corpus'; it is now 'is never a request\nactor at all' - search, read AND the two browse routes refuse a caller presenting the shared org id (403,\nuniform message). Nothing is lost: every org still searches and reads the corpus, and each hit/document\nsays scope:'org'|'shared' while the underlying orgId never reaches the wire.\nAUDIT: the two NEW routes write ONE activity row + ONE structured console line per call through the single\naudit path (category 'knowledge', verdict ok|denied|not_found|forbidden|error, keyId+xClient on a key\ncall), refusals included. The query TEXT and the document body are deliberately NOT recorded - a search\nstring here is a client's confidential matter; the row carries the call's shape, not its content.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (knowledge search/read over REST, slice E5): the knowledge domain gains a CAPABILITY\nREAD surface. NOTHING moves in knowledge/ itself - the org-partitioned vault + FTS5 index are unchanged,\nand the in-process agent path (server.ts setKnowledgeToolSearch/setKnowledgeToolRead -> agents/) is\nuntouched. What changes is REACH: routes/knowledge.ts now has TWO admission tiers in ONE router.\nTIER 1 (mounted BEFORE the router-wide requireAuth, so express's middleware order is what separates the\ntiers - the same shape automations.ts uses for its SSE route): GET /collections, GET /documents,\nNEW POST /search, NEW GET /documents/:collection/:docId, all requireUserOrApiKey / auth:'user-or-key'.\nTIER 2 (after r.use(requireAuth)): ingest, delete, sources, uploads, reindex, index-status - platform\nsession ONLY. This slice opens NO ingestion surface to a key; requireAuth refuses an ekoa_gk_ bearer as an\nunparseable JWT, which the contract suite pins on all eight write/admin routes.\nTHE TWO NEW ROUTES REUSE, THEY DO NOT REIMPLEMENT: service.searchDocuments wraps index-store.search - the\nSAME function the agent tool seam calls, org partitioning in its signature - and service.readDocument wraps\nreadDocWithShared (own vault shadows the shared corpus). A `collection` filter narrows AFTER the FTS query\n(the index has no collection predicate and gaining one would change the shape agents/ depends on), so a\nfiltered search over-fetches and is a relevance-ordered narrowing, stated in-code, not a WHERE scan.\nORG SCOPE IS STRUCTURAL: it rides actorOf(req)/the audited ActivityActor and nothing else. No knowledge\nschema declares an org/tenant field, zod strips unknown keys, and a grep gate in the new scoping suite\nbans reading an org out of req.body/query/params/headers anywhere in knowledge/ or routes/knowledge.ts.\nPATH SHAPE: a collection and a docId are each ONE vault segment (shared/ KnowledgeSegment mirrors paths.ts\nSEGMENT_RE, '.'/'..' refused), so '/' is unrepresentable and two ordinary express :params suffice - no\nwildcard and no ?permalink= workaround as memvault's multi-segment permalinks needed.\n`_shared` TIGHTENS: assertNotSharedActor was 'cannot MUTATE the corpus'; it is now 'is never a request\nactor at all' - search, read AND the two browse routes refuse a caller presenting the shared org id (403,\nuniform message). Nothing is lost: every org still searches and reads the corpus, and each hit/document\nsays scope:'org'|'shared' while the underlying orgId never reaches the wire.\nAUDIT: the two NEW routes write ONE activity row + ONE structured console line per call through the single\naudit path (category 'knowledge', verdict ok|denied|not_found|forbidden|error, keyId+xClient on a key\ncall), refusals included. The query TEXT and the document body are deliberately NOT recorded - a search\nstring here is a client's confidential matter; the row carries the call's shape, not its content.",
