  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-consent-once-20260731",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 8180,
   "width": 916,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (local_command consent, both answers): the consent gate now has TWO stores,\nand the difference between them IS the difference between the two answers the dialog offers.\n\n\"Sempre\" -> consent.ts approvedCommands, keyed owner+org+MACHINE with a 90-day TTL (J-7). The\nscope is recorded on the run ConsentRequest BY THE EXECUTOR THAT ASKS\n(executors/local-command.ts) and read back by service.ts resolveConsent - never re-derived,\nbecause the executor re-reads that exact key on the retry, and a resolver guessing pairingId:null\nwrote a row that lookup could never see.\n\n\"Uma vez\" -> RunContext.runApprovedShapes, a Set on the in-memory signal record in service.ts,\nchecked BEFORE the durable store so a one-off answer never touches it. It dies with the run, so a\nrestart re-asks - the safe direction. Before it existed, once persisted nothing (correct) and had\nnowhere to be remembered: the step re-ran, re-read the durable store, found nothing and asked\nagain - a loop whose only exits were the two answers the user had just declined to give.\n\nBOTH answers bind to the shape the run is AWAITING; a caller-supplied shape is FORBIDDEN in\neither case. Tier unchanged: automation/ (5) -> data/ (0). No new module, no new edge on this map.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (local_command consent, both answers): the consent gate now has TWO stores,\nand the difference between them IS the difference between the two answers the dialog offers.\n\n\"Sempre\" -> consent.ts approvedCommands, keyed owner+org+MACHINE with a 90-day TTL (J-7). The\nscope is recorded on the run ConsentRequest BY THE EXECUTOR THAT ASKS\n(executors/local-command.ts) and read back by service.ts resolveConsent - never re-derived,\nbecause the executor re-reads that exact key on the retry, and a resolver guessing pairingId:null\nwrote a row that lookup could never see.\n\n\"Uma vez\" -> RunContext.runApprovedShapes, a Set on the in-memory signal record in service.ts,\nchecked BEFORE the durable store so a one-off answer never touches it. It dies with the run, so a\nrestart re-asks - the safe direction. Before it existed, once persisted nothing (correct) and had\nnowhere to be remembered: the step re-ran, re-read the durable store, found nothing and asked\nagain - a loop whose only exits were the two answers the user had just declined to give.\n\nBOTH answers bind to the shape the run is AWAITING; a caller-supplied shape is FORBIDDEN in\neither case. Tier unchanged: automation/ (5) -> data/ (0). No new module, no new edge on this map.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (local_command consent, both answers): the consent gate now has TWO stores,\nand the difference between them IS the difference between the two answers the dialog offers.\n\n\"Sempre\" -> consent.ts approvedCommands, keyed owner+org+MACHINE with a 90-day TTL (J-7). The\nscope is recorded on the run ConsentRequest BY THE EXECUTOR THAT ASKS\n(executors/local-command.ts) and read back by service.ts resolveConsent - never re-derived,\nbecause the executor re-reads that exact key on the retry, and a resolver guessing pairingId:null\nwrote a row that lookup could never see.\n\n\"Uma vez\" -> RunContext.runApprovedShapes, a Set on the in-memory signal record in service.ts,\nchecked BEFORE the durable store so a one-off answer never touches it. It dies with the run, so a\nrestart re-asks - the safe direction. Before it existed, once persisted nothing (correct) and had\nnowhere to be remembered: the step re-ran, re-read the durable store, found nothing and asked\nagain - a loop whose only exits were the two answers the user had just declined to give.\n\nBOTH answers bind to the shape the run is AWAITING; a caller-supplied shape is FORBIDDEN in\neither case. Tier unchanged: automation/ (5) -> data/ (0). No new module, no new edge on this map.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 551903774,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 551903775,
