  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-integration-agent-20260803",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 8900,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 367.5,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (one authoring core, slice D2 + re-review): NEW api/src/agents/authoring-core.ts -\nthe authoring core the integration BUILDER and the automation PLANNER share. Both carried their own copy\nof the same four steps around one model call: compose the system prompt as [content sections ..., output\ncontract] with the contract LAST, run ONE tool-less turn through the chokepoint with an attribution tag,\nclassify the outcome (text | transport failure | EMPTY reply | deliberate abort), and re-emit once with\nthe violations fed back. The core owns exactly those four; composeAuthoringPrompt + authorWithRepair are\nits whole surface and llm/ is its ONLY import - a property of the FILE since the re-review (LOW-1) split\nit out of agents/integration-agent.ts, which as the builder's ADAPTER also pulls in billing/, the agent\nseams and the builder session store (hence the Mongo store registry) that the planner was transitively\nloading. Per-caller, as typed seams, never branched on inside the core: output FORMAT + validation\nvocabulary (parse), turn text incl. repair wording (userText), tier/attribution, persistence, the wire.\nNEW EDGE, and the FIRST between two tier-5 modules: automation/planner.ts -> agents/authoring-core.ts.\nIt runs ONE WAY and that is now a lint zone (.eslintrc.cjs: agents/ must not import automation/), because\nthe tier table's acyclicity is the whole safety argument for a sibling import. Not a seam: a seam causes\nwork in a collaborator and is wired at the composition root - this is a library dependency on a pure\nfunction pair, and hiding it behind indirection would make a static dependency invisible.\nagents/integration-builder.ts keeps ONLY the session store (persistence is per-caller); routes/\nintegration-builder.ts calls handleBuilderChat from the ADAPTER and its wire is byte-unchanged - same\nshapes, status codes, envelope, proven by the pre-existing contract suite passing UNMODIFIED plus two new\npins: a 500 INTERNAL on an egress THROW, a package-less 200 on an EMPTY MODEL REPLY (two outcomes the D2\njournal entry conflated - erratum in docs/decisions.md).",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (one authoring core, slice D2 + re-review): NEW api/src/agents/authoring-core.ts -\nthe authoring core the integration BUILDER and the automation PLANNER share. Both carried their own copy\nof the same four steps around one model call: compose the system prompt as [content sections ..., output\ncontract] with the contract LAST, run ONE tool-less turn through the chokepoint with an attribution tag,\nclassify the outcome (text | transport failure | EMPTY reply | deliberate abort), and re-emit once with\nthe violations fed back. The core owns exactly those four; composeAuthoringPrompt + authorWithRepair are\nits whole surface and llm/ is its ONLY import - a property of the FILE since the re-review (LOW-1) split\nit out of agents/integration-agent.ts, which as the builder's ADAPTER also pulls in billing/, the agent\nseams and the builder session store (hence the Mongo store registry) that the planner was transitively\nloading. Per-caller, as typed seams, never branched on inside the core: output FORMAT + validation\nvocabulary (parse), turn text incl. repair wording (userText), tier/attribution, persistence, the wire.\nNEW EDGE, and the FIRST between two tier-5 modules: automation/planner.ts -> agents/authoring-core.ts.\nIt runs ONE WAY and that is now a lint zone (.eslintrc.cjs: agents/ must not import automation/), because\nthe tier table's acyclicity is the whole safety argument for a sibling import. Not a seam: a seam causes\nwork in a collaborator and is wired at the composition root - this is a library dependency on a pure\nfunction pair, and hiding it behind indirection would make a static dependency invisible.\nagents/integration-builder.ts keeps ONLY the session store (persistence is per-caller); routes/\nintegration-builder.ts calls handleBuilderChat from the ADAPTER and its wire is byte-unchanged - same\nshapes, status codes, envelope, proven by the pre-existing contract suite passing UNMODIFIED plus two new\npins: a 500 INTERNAL on an egress THROW, a package-less 200 on an EMPTY MODEL REPLY (two outcomes the D2\njournal entry conflated - erratum in docs/decisions.md).",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (one authoring core, slice D2 + re-review): NEW api/src/agents/authoring-core.ts -\nthe authoring core the integration BUILDER and the automation PLANNER share. Both carried their own copy\nof the same four steps around one model call: compose the system prompt as [content sections ..., output\ncontract] with the contract LAST, run ONE tool-less turn through the chokepoint with an attribution tag,\nclassify the outcome (text | transport failure | EMPTY reply | deliberate abort), and re-emit once with\nthe violations fed back. The core owns exactly those four; composeAuthoringPrompt + authorWithRepair are\nits whole surface and llm/ is its ONLY import - a property of the FILE since the re-review (LOW-1) split\nit out of agents/integration-agent.ts, which as the builder's ADAPTER also pulls in billing/, the agent\nseams and the builder session store (hence the Mongo store registry) that the planner was transitively\nloading. Per-caller, as typed seams, never branched on inside the core: output FORMAT + validation\nvocabulary (parse), turn text incl. repair wording (userText), tier/attribution, persistence, the wire.\nNEW EDGE, and the FIRST between two tier-5 modules: automation/planner.ts -> agents/authoring-core.ts.\nIt runs ONE WAY and that is now a lint zone (.eslintrc.cjs: agents/ must not import automation/), because\nthe tier table's acyclicity is the whole safety argument for a sibling import. Not a seam: a seam causes\nwork in a collaborator and is wired at the composition root - this is a library dependency on a pure\nfunction pair, and hiding it behind indirection would make a static dependency invisible.\nagents/integration-builder.ts keeps ONLY the session store (persistence is per-caller); routes/\nintegration-builder.ts calls handleBuilderChat from the ADAPTER and its wire is byte-unchanged - same\nshapes, status codes, envelope, proven by the pre-existing contract suite passing UNMODIFIED plus two new\npins: a 500 INTERNAL on an egress THROW, a package-less 200 on an EMPTY MODEL REPLY (two outcomes the D2\njournal entry conflated - erratum in docs/decisions.md).",
