   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-05 (ekoa-dev parity run) - THE WORKSPACE PLANES GO LIVE, PER OWNER.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/workspace-credential.ts (tier 3, integrations/). The served-app workspace\nplanes - m365-proxy.ts (ALL /api/m365/*) and app-cloud-files.ts (/api/app-cloud-files/*) - were\nmounted against a seam server.ts bound to a permanent `not connected` thrower, so both were gated,\ntested and inert. This module is what the seam now resolves to.\n\nTHE RULE IT ENCODES: the workspace of a served app is THE ORG OF ITS OWNER. platform-OAuth rows are\norg-scoped (platform-<orgId>-<provider>), so there is no ambient process-wide connection to reach\nfor (the old platform had one; this repo must not). Per request: appId -> ownerUserId (from the app\nscope the router ALREADY admitted) -> orgId (injected users lookup) -> getValidPlatformTokens, which\nrefreshes + re-persists behind the seam.\n\nSEAM SIGNATURES GREW AN OWNER, deliberately:\n  m365-proxy      getWorkspaceGraphToken(ownerUserId)\n  app-cloud-files getStatus(ownerUserId) / getAccessToken(provider, ownerUserId)\nA workspace token with no subject is an ambient identity - Capability Contract rules 4 + 5. The owner\nis the ADMITTED app's, never the X-Ekoa-App-Id spelling and never the caller's JWT (pinned in\ntests/contract/app-sso.test.ts). Empty/unknown/org-less owner => resolves NOBODY, with zero provider\ntraffic. Honest degrade unchanged: `not connected` -> 409 (cloud-files) / 502 (Graph proxy).\n\nIMPORTS: platform-oauth (token custody) + app-cloud-files (the CloudFilesStatus/CloudProvider types).\nIt does NOT import data/ or auth/ - resolveOwnerOrgId is injected by server.ts, the same shape\ncredentialReadDeps already uses. No new edge out of integrations/.\n\nSTILL STUBBED, ON PURPOSE: integrations/docx-fetch.ts keeps the not-connected binding. Its cloud\nbranch is reached from a BUILD through agents/seams.ts fetchFromCloud, which carries an appId but no\nowner, and guessing whose credential to spend there is the ambient identity this replaces. Threading\nthe run's owner through that seam is logged open in docs/dev-parity.md.\n\nALSO THIS RUN (no map change, recorded for the reader): apps/manifest.ts carries m365Proxy through\nvalidation (it was stripped by the whitelist, so the proxy's per-app opt-in could never be granted);\nintegrations/service.ts gains mergeCredentialValues + upsertConfig, so a credential save merges into\nthe stored bundle and the dashboard's save updates its row instead of forking a duplicate.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-05 (ekoa-dev parity run) - THE WORKSPACE PLANES GO LIVE, PER OWNER.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/workspace-credential.ts (tier 3, integrations/). The served-app workspace\nplanes - m365-proxy.ts (ALL /api/m365/*) and app-cloud-files.ts (/api/app-cloud-files/*) - were\nmounted against a seam server.ts bound to a permanent `not connected` thrower, so both were gated,\ntested and inert. This module is what the seam now resolves to.\n\nTHE RULE IT ENCODES: the workspace of a served app is THE ORG OF ITS OWNER. platform-OAuth rows are\norg-scoped (platform-<orgId>-<provider>), so there is no ambient process-wide connection to reach\nfor (the old platform had one; this repo must not). Per request: appId -> ownerUserId (from the app\nscope the router ALREADY admitted) -> orgId (injected users lookup) -> getValidPlatformTokens, which\nrefreshes + re-persists behind the seam.\n\nSEAM SIGNATURES GREW AN OWNER, deliberately:\n  m365-proxy      getWorkspaceGraphToken(ownerUserId)\n  app-cloud-files getStatus(ownerUserId) / getAccessToken(provider, ownerUserId)\nA workspace token with no subject is an ambient identity - Capability Contract rules 4 + 5. The owner\nis the ADMITTED app's, never the X-Ekoa-App-Id spelling and never the caller's JWT (pinned in\ntests/contract/app-sso.test.ts). Empty/unknown/org-less owner => resolves NOBODY, with zero provider\ntraffic. Honest degrade unchanged: `not connected` -> 409 (cloud-files) / 502 (Graph proxy).\n\nIMPORTS: platform-oauth (token custody) + app-cloud-files (the CloudFilesStatus/CloudProvider types).\nIt does NOT import data/ or auth/ - resolveOwnerOrgId is injected by server.ts, the same shape\ncredentialReadDeps already uses. No new edge out of integrations/.\n\nSTILL STUBBED, ON PURPOSE: integrations/docx-fetch.ts keeps the not-connected binding. Its cloud\nbranch is reached from a BUILD through agents/seams.ts fetchFromCloud, which carries an appId but no\nowner, and guessing whose credential to spend there is the ambient identity this replaces. Threading\nthe run's owner through that seam is logged open in docs/dev-parity.md.\n\nALSO THIS RUN (no map change, recorded for the reader): apps/manifest.ts carries m365Proxy through\nvalidation (it was stripped by the whitelist, so the proxy's per-app opt-in could never be granted);\nintegrations/service.ts gains mergeCredentialValues + upsertConfig, so a credential save merges into\nthe stored bundle and the dashboard's save updates its row instead of forking a duplicate.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-05 (ekoa-dev parity run) - THE WORKSPACE PLANES GO LIVE, PER OWNER.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/workspace-credential.ts (tier 3, integrations/). The served-app workspace\nplanes - m365-proxy.ts (ALL /api/m365/*) and app-cloud-files.ts (/api/app-cloud-files/*) - were\nmounted against a seam server.ts bound to a permanent `not connected` thrower, so both were gated,\ntested and inert. This module is what the seam now resolves to.\n\nTHE RULE IT ENCODES: the workspace of a served app is THE ORG OF ITS OWNER. platform-OAuth rows are\norg-scoped (platform-<orgId>-<provider>), so there is no ambient process-wide connection to reach\nfor (the old platform had one; this repo must not). Per request: appId -> ownerUserId (from the app\nscope the router ALREADY admitted) -> orgId (injected users lookup) -> getValidPlatformTokens, which\nrefreshes + re-persists behind the seam.\n\nSEAM SIGNATURES GREW AN OWNER, deliberately:\n  m365-proxy      getWorkspaceGraphToken(ownerUserId)\n  app-cloud-files getStatus(ownerUserId) / getAccessToken(provider, ownerUserId)\nA workspace token with no subject is an ambient identity - Capability Contract rules 4 + 5. The owner\nis the ADMITTED app's, never the X-Ekoa-App-Id spelling and never the caller's JWT (pinned in\ntests/contract/app-sso.test.ts). Empty/unknown/org-less owner => resolves NOBODY, with zero provider\ntraffic. Honest degrade unchanged: `not connected` -> 409 (cloud-files) / 502 (Graph proxy).\n\nIMPORTS: platform-oauth (token custody) + app-cloud-files (the CloudFilesStatus/CloudProvider types).\nIt does NOT import data/ or auth/ - resolveOwnerOrgId is injected by server.ts, the same shape\ncredentialReadDeps already uses. No new edge out of integrations/.\n\nSTILL STUBBED, ON PURPOSE: integrations/docx-fetch.ts keeps the not-connected binding. Its cloud\nbranch is reached from a BUILD through agents/seams.ts fetchFromCloud, which carries an appId but no\nowner, and guessing whose credential to spend there is the ambient identity this replaces. Threading\nthe run's owner through that seam is logged open in docs/dev-parity.md.\n\nALSO THIS RUN (no map change, recorded for the reader): apps/manifest.ts carries m365Proxy through\nvalidation (it was stripped by the whitelist, so the proxy's per-app opt-in could never be granted);\nintegrations/service.ts gains mergeCredentialValues + upsertConfig, so a credential save merges into\nthe stored bundle and the dashboard's save updates its row instead of forking a duplicate.",
