  {
   "type": "text",
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 202608182,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "id": "asbuilt-20260818-p20-recipe-modules",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "x": 60,
   "y": 15462.0,
   "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "width": 1080,
   "height": 350.0,
   "seed": 202608183,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1755500000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): THREE new modules, split by tier.\nNEW api/src/automation/recipe.ts (tier 5): the ENGINE-side compiled recipe - CompiledRecipe /\nInjectedCall / ScriptedStep, which EXTEND the stored interfaces in integrations/definitions.ts and\nnarrow method/locator/action back to ApiCallMethod / Locator / PlaywrightAction['kind'], so the\npersisted shape and the engine shape cannot drift (compile-checked, type-only, DOWN the tier table).\nIt owns the \"names, never values\" fence: HeaderName is a BRANDED string whose only constructors are\nheaderNameOf (RFC 7230 token grammar + a 64-char bound) and injectedCallFromExchange (handed the live\nheader map, reads its KEYS), plus parseCompiledRecipe, which re-validates a stored recipe before any\nreplay and answers null rather than half-understanding one.\nNEW api/src/integrations/recipe-store.ts (tier 3): the ONE writer of a recipe, over the EXISTING\nintegration_definitions collection (the recipe folds onto the action). putRecipe / supersedeRecipe /\ngetRecipe / getRecipeForActor / listRecipes / listRecipesForActor; version is store-owned;\nassertCarriesNoValues REFUSES (never redacts) a recipe carrying a header value, a secret-shaped\nliteral (publish-scrub's looksLikeLiteralSecret, reused not re-derived) or any value in the run's\nSecretRegistry.\nNEW api/src/integrations/captured-calls-store.ts (tier 3): the RAW evidence, in its own collection\n(see 05-data-model). Both stores import security/redaction.ts (tier 2b) and data/ (tier 0) only -\nintegrations/ still imports nothing from automation/, and automation/recipe.ts's single edge into\nintegrations/ is a TYPE-ONLY import that is erased at compile time.\nDiscovery, capture, the replay executor and self-heal (P2.1-P2.4) are NOT in this slice.",
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): THREE new modules, split by tier.\nNEW api/src/automation/recipe.ts (tier 5): the ENGINE-side compiled recipe - CompiledRecipe /\nInjectedCall / ScriptedStep, which EXTEND the stored interfaces in integrations/definitions.ts and\nnarrow method/locator/action back to ApiCallMethod / Locator / PlaywrightAction['kind'], so the\npersisted shape and the engine shape cannot drift (compile-checked, type-only, DOWN the tier table).\nIt owns the \"names, never values\" fence: HeaderName is a BRANDED string whose only constructors are\nheaderNameOf (RFC 7230 token grammar + a 64-char bound) and injectedCallFromExchange (handed the live\nheader map, reads its KEYS), plus parseCompiledRecipe, which re-validates a stored recipe before any\nreplay and answers null rather than half-understanding one.\nNEW api/src/integrations/recipe-store.ts (tier 3): the ONE writer of a recipe, over the EXISTING\nintegration_definitions collection (the recipe folds onto the action). putRecipe / supersedeRecipe /\ngetRecipe / getRecipeForActor / listRecipes / listRecipesForActor; version is store-owned;\nassertCarriesNoValues REFUSES (never redacts) a recipe carrying a header value, a secret-shaped\nliteral (publish-scrub's looksLikeLiteralSecret, reused not re-derived) or any value in the run's\nSecretRegistry.\nNEW api/src/integrations/captured-calls-store.ts (tier 3): the RAW evidence, in its own collection\n(see 05-data-model). Both stores import security/redaction.ts (tier 2b) and data/ (tier 0) only -\nintegrations/ still imports nothing from automation/, and automation/recipe.ts's single edge into\nintegrations/ is a TYPE-ONLY import that is erased at compile time.\nDiscovery, capture, the replay executor and self-heal (P2.1-P2.4) are NOT in this slice.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): THREE new modules, split by tier.\nNEW api/src/automation/recipe.ts (tier 5): the ENGINE-side compiled recipe - CompiledRecipe /\nInjectedCall / ScriptedStep, which EXTEND the stored interfaces in integrations/definitions.ts and\nnarrow method/locator/action back to ApiCallMethod / Locator / PlaywrightAction['kind'], so the\npersisted shape and the engine shape cannot drift (compile-checked, type-only, DOWN the tier table).\nIt owns the \"names, never values\" fence: HeaderName is a BRANDED string whose only constructors are\nheaderNameOf (RFC 7230 token grammar + a 64-char bound) and injectedCallFromExchange (handed the live\nheader map, reads its KEYS), plus parseCompiledRecipe, which re-validates a stored recipe before any\nreplay and answers null rather than half-understanding one.\nNEW api/src/integrations/recipe-store.ts (tier 3): the ONE writer of a recipe, over the EXISTING\nintegration_definitions collection (the recipe folds onto the action). putRecipe / supersedeRecipe /\ngetRecipe / getRecipeForActor / listRecipes / listRecipesForActor; version is store-owned;\nassertCarriesNoValues REFUSES (never redacts) a recipe carrying a header value, a secret-shaped\nliteral (publish-scrub's looksLikeLiteralSecret, reused not re-derived) or any value in the run's\nSecretRegistry.\nNEW api/src/integrations/captured-calls-store.ts (tier 3): the RAW evidence, in its own collection\n(see 05-data-model). Both stores import security/redaction.ts (tier 2b) and data/ (tier 0) only -\nintegrations/ still imports nothing from automation/, and automation/recipe.ts's single edge into\nintegrations/ is a TYPE-ONLY import that is erased at compile time.\nDiscovery, capture, the replay executor and self-heal (P2.1-P2.4) are NOT in this slice.",
