   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P1: the bridge execution plane - three new daemon modules, one new Cortex seam).\n\nclients/bridge/src/browser/  (NEW)\n  profile.ts   ProfileManager: chromium.launchPersistentContext under <EKOA_BRIDGE_HOME>/profiles/<id>\n               at 0700 - NEVER the user's real Chrome directory. Per-profileId async mutex (a second\n               run QUEUES; Chromium refuses a second launch against a live userDataDir), stale\n               SingletonLock cleanup, session INJECTED per run from the Cofre and CLEARED at run end.\n  executor.ts  The PlaywrightAction vocabulary, port-with-review of api/src/automation/executor.ts,\n               plus the observation (url/title/heading/domShapeSketch/a11y/viewport + screenshot).\n               The six verbs browser-session.ts listed as unsupported are reconciled here.\n  types.ts     The slice of Playwright the plane uses, as interfaces - so the unit lane substitutes a\n               fake and NO unit test needs a display.\n\nclients/bridge/src/runtime/  (EXTENDED)\n  tool-executor.ts     the two gates, the dispatch, the ledgered refusals.\n  secret-hold.ts       RAM-only credential custody, values as Buffers, zeroized in a finally + on TTL.\n  outbound-redactor.ts value-keyed EGRESS filter; wraps send once inside DaemonRuntime.\n\nclients/bridge/src/tools/tier2/bash.ts  (EXTENDED)\n  bashArgv(): argv, NO SHELL, and a cwd resolved through the SINGLE containment resolver against the\n  step's grant root. Before this a bash step ran with the daemon's own process cwd and no\n  containment at all - it could cd anywhere on the machine. eslint's FS_OWNING_GLOBS gains\n  src/browser/** so the realpath half of the single-resolver ban still applies there.\n\napi/src/bridge/daemon-step-seam.ts  (NEW)\n  The one place a resolved step becomes a tool.invoke: capability map, screenshot threading, and the\n  authorise -> deliver -> invoke order under ONE invocationId. Extracted from server.ts precisely so\n  it can be imported and asserted - three defects lived in those six inline lines.\n\nshared/src/ekoa-local.ts  (ADDITIVE)\n  LocalBrowserLocator / LocalBrowserAction / LocalBrowserStepInput / LocalBashStepInput /\n  LocalToolInvokeInput / LocalBrowserObservation / LocalBashObservation, plus the optional\n  screenshotB64 on tool.result. Both ends parse the same objects, so a step Cortex sends and a step\n  the daemon runs cannot drift apart.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P1: the bridge execution plane - three new daemon modules, one new Cortex seam).\n\nclients/bridge/src/browser/  (NEW)\n  profile.ts   ProfileManager: chromium.launchPersistentContext under <EKOA_BRIDGE_HOME>/profiles/<id>\n               at 0700 - NEVER the user's real Chrome directory. Per-profileId async mutex (a second\n               run QUEUES; Chromium refuses a second launch against a live userDataDir), stale\n               SingletonLock cleanup, session INJECTED per run from the Cofre and CLEARED at run end.\n  executor.ts  The PlaywrightAction vocabulary, port-with-review of api/src/automation/executor.ts,\n               plus the observation (url/title/heading/domShapeSketch/a11y/viewport + screenshot).\n               The six verbs browser-session.ts listed as unsupported are reconciled here.\n  types.ts     The slice of Playwright the plane uses, as interfaces - so the unit lane substitutes a\n               fake and NO unit test needs a display.\n\nclients/bridge/src/runtime/  (EXTENDED)\n  tool-executor.ts     the two gates, the dispatch, the ledgered refusals.\n  secret-hold.ts       RAM-only credential custody, values as Buffers, zeroized in a finally + on TTL.\n  outbound-redactor.ts value-keyed EGRESS filter; wraps send once inside DaemonRuntime.\n\nclients/bridge/src/tools/tier2/bash.ts  (EXTENDED)\n  bashArgv(): argv, NO SHELL, and a cwd resolved through the SINGLE containment resolver against the\n  step's grant root. Before this a bash step ran with the daemon's own process cwd and no\n  containment at all - it could cd anywhere on the machine. eslint's FS_OWNING_GLOBS gains\n  src/browser/** so the realpath half of the single-resolver ban still applies there.\n\napi/src/bridge/daemon-step-seam.ts  (NEW)\n  The one place a resolved step becomes a tool.invoke: capability map, screenshot threading, and the\n  authorise -> deliver -> invoke order under ONE invocationId. Extracted from server.ts precisely so\n  it can be imported and asserted - three defects lived in those six inline lines.\n\nshared/src/ekoa-local.ts  (ADDITIVE)\n  LocalBrowserLocator / LocalBrowserAction / LocalBrowserStepInput / LocalBashStepInput /\n  LocalToolInvokeInput / LocalBrowserObservation / LocalBashObservation, plus the optional\n  screenshotB64 on tool.result. Both ends parse the same objects, so a step Cortex sends and a step\n  the daemon runs cannot drift apart.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P1: the bridge execution plane - three new daemon modules, one new Cortex seam).\n\nclients/bridge/src/browser/  (NEW)\n  profile.ts   ProfileManager: chromium.launchPersistentContext under <EKOA_BRIDGE_HOME>/profiles/<id>\n               at 0700 - NEVER the user's real Chrome directory. Per-profileId async mutex (a second\n               run QUEUES; Chromium refuses a second launch against a live userDataDir), stale\n               SingletonLock cleanup, session INJECTED per run from the Cofre and CLEARED at run end.\n  executor.ts  The PlaywrightAction vocabulary, port-with-review of api/src/automation/executor.ts,\n               plus the observation (url/title/heading/domShapeSketch/a11y/viewport + screenshot).\n               The six verbs browser-session.ts listed as unsupported are reconciled here.\n  types.ts     The slice of Playwright the plane uses, as interfaces - so the unit lane substitutes a\n               fake and NO unit test needs a display.\n\nclients/bridge/src/runtime/  (EXTENDED)\n  tool-executor.ts     the two gates, the dispatch, the ledgered refusals.\n  secret-hold.ts       RAM-only credential custody, values as Buffers, zeroized in a finally + on TTL.\n  outbound-redactor.ts value-keyed EGRESS filter; wraps send once inside DaemonRuntime.\n\nclients/bridge/src/tools/tier2/bash.ts  (EXTENDED)\n  bashArgv(): argv, NO SHELL, and a cwd resolved through the SINGLE containment resolver against the\n  step's grant root. Before this a bash step ran with the daemon's own process cwd and no\n  containment at all - it could cd anywhere on the machine. eslint's FS_OWNING_GLOBS gains\n  src/browser/** so the realpath half of the single-resolver ban still applies there.\n\napi/src/bridge/daemon-step-seam.ts  (NEW)\n  The one place a resolved step becomes a tool.invoke: capability map, screenshot threading, and the\n  authorise -> deliver -> invoke order under ONE invocationId. Extracted from server.ts precisely so\n  it can be imported and asserted - three defects lived in those six inline lines.\n\nshared/src/ekoa-local.ts  (ADDITIVE)\n  LocalBrowserLocator / LocalBrowserAction / LocalBrowserStepInput / LocalBashStepInput /\n  LocalToolInvokeInput / LocalBrowserObservation / LocalBashObservation, plus the optional\n  screenshotB64 on tool.result. Both ends parse the same objects, so a step Cortex sends and a step\n  the daemon runs cannot drift apart."
  },
