   "type": "text",
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1455684688,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "id": "asbuilt-20260819-p2-discovery-spine",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "x": 60,
   "y": 18694.5,
   "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "width": 947.1,
   "height": 577.5,
   "seed": 559058691,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 - P2.1-P2.4: the discovery -> capture -> replay -> self-heal spine.\n\nTHE INVERSION. A browser-steps action re-derived its whole flow, vision-first, on every run. It now does that ONCE:\ndiscovery drives the page from a GOAL while the machine records what the page's own JavaScript asks the server for,\nand the distilled recipe of those calls is replayed by every later run with NO model in the loop.\n\nNEW MODULES (api/src/automation/)\n  discovery.ts             the goal loop. A SIBLING of runOrRehearse, not a reuse: rehearsal PATCHES a step list and its\n                           fixer may only local-patch the current index; discovery has no list and AUTHORS a recipe.\n                           It composes BrowserSession, the vision resolver, the fixer (for one failed act) and\n                           SecretRegistry, and adds the goal loop + the DISCOVERY_BUDGET re-plan/step/wall-clock caps.\n  discovery-goal-verify.ts the RUN-level gate. One EXPERT verify against the goal PLUS the captured evidence (call count\n                           and the value-free SHAPE of the last answer). Without it a pass compiles a recipe off a\n                           login wall. Reused verbatim by the heal.\n  network-capture.ts       the hosted redaction boundary + the model-free learner: redactCaptures -> internalApiCalls\n                           -> compileInjectedCalls / deriveLessons. Compiling needs no LLM, which is WHY run 2 is free.\n  response-shape.ts        expectShape: kinds and key names, never values. Drift = a key that DISAPPEARED, never one added.\n  executors/injected-call.ts  the replay ladder: in-page fetch -> node HTTP (PERMISSIVE origins only) -> scripted DOM.\n                           Vision is NOT a rung - it is the caller's fall-through, so a replay cannot silently cost tokens.\n  replay-action.ts         the MOUNT. Reads the recipe through recipe-store (ORG-SCOPED) - never through the definition\n                           projection, which strips recipes so they cannot reach the wire.\n  discovery-service.ts     the phase entry: run a pass, write evidence, then the recipe that points at it.\n  self-heal.ts             drift -> re-discover -> supersedeRecipe (tenant-scoped, version bumped, lineage stamped).\n                           NEVER publishSnapshot: its gate is super-admin AND it flips the row to global.\n\nWHERE IT MOUNTS. automation/service.ts runAutomationForAction tries the recipe BEFORE running the automation. Every\noutcome except ok and write-gate falls THROUGH to the old path, so the worst case is the run as it was before P2.\nwrite-gate does not fall through - a non-idempotent replay stops for a human (trap T4) and routing around it would\nmake the gate decorative. action-executor.ts passes integrationKey/actionName additively for that lookup.\n\nTHE MACHINE HALF (clients/bridge/src/browser/). capture.ts records request/response pairs, keeps header NAMES, and\nholds the live header VALUES in memory for the lease so inject.ts can forward them into an in-page fetch. Values never\ncross the wire in either direction: the LocalBrowserCapture / LocalBrowserInjectedCall schemas have no field for one.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 - P2.1-P2.4: the discovery -> capture -> replay -> self-heal spine.\n\nTHE INVERSION. A browser-steps action re-derived its whole flow, vision-first, on every run. It now does that ONCE:\ndiscovery drives the page from a GOAL while the machine records what the page's own JavaScript asks the server for,\nand the distilled recipe of those calls is replayed by every later run with NO model in the loop.\n\nNEW MODULES (api/src/automation/)\n  discovery.ts             the goal loop. A SIBLING of runOrRehearse, not a reuse: rehearsal PATCHES a step list and its\n                           fixer may only local-patch the current index; discovery has no list and AUTHORS a recipe.\n                           It composes BrowserSession, the vision resolver, the fixer (for one failed act) and\n                           SecretRegistry, and adds the goal loop + the DISCOVERY_BUDGET re-plan/step/wall-clock caps.\n  discovery-goal-verify.ts the RUN-level gate. One EXPERT verify against the goal PLUS the captured evidence (call count\n                           and the value-free SHAPE of the last answer). Without it a pass compiles a recipe off a\n                           login wall. Reused verbatim by the heal.\n  network-capture.ts       the hosted redaction boundary + the model-free learner: redactCaptures -> internalApiCalls\n                           -> compileInjectedCalls / deriveLessons. Compiling needs no LLM, which is WHY run 2 is free.\n  response-shape.ts        expectShape: kinds and key names, never values. Drift = a key that DISAPPEARED, never one added.\n  executors/injected-call.ts  the replay ladder: in-page fetch -> node HTTP (PERMISSIVE origins only) -> scripted DOM.\n                           Vision is NOT a rung - it is the caller's fall-through, so a replay cannot silently cost tokens.\n  replay-action.ts         the MOUNT. Reads the recipe through recipe-store (ORG-SCOPED) - never through the definition\n                           projection, which strips recipes so they cannot reach the wire.\n  discovery-service.ts     the phase entry: run a pass, write evidence, then the recipe that points at it.\n  self-heal.ts             drift -> re-discover -> supersedeRecipe (tenant-scoped, version bumped, lineage stamped).\n                           NEVER publishSnapshot: its gate is super-admin AND it flips the row to global.\n\nWHERE IT MOUNTS. automation/service.ts runAutomationForAction tries the recipe BEFORE running the automation. Every\noutcome except ok and write-gate falls THROUGH to the old path, so the worst case is the run as it was before P2.\nwrite-gate does not fall through - a non-idempotent replay stops for a human (trap T4) and routing around it would\nmake the gate decorative. action-executor.ts passes integrationKey/actionName additively for that lookup.\n\nTHE MACHINE HALF (clients/bridge/src/browser/). capture.ts records request/response pairs, keeps header NAMES, and\nholds the live header VALUES in memory for the lease so inject.ts can forward them into an in-page fetch. Values never\ncross the wire in either direction: the LocalBrowserCapture / LocalBrowserInjectedCall schemas have no field for one.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 - P2.1-P2.4: the discovery -> capture -> replay -> self-heal spine.\n\nTHE INVERSION. A browser-steps action re-derived its whole flow, vision-first, on every run. It now does that ONCE:\ndiscovery drives the page from a GOAL while the machine records what the page's own JavaScript asks the server for,\nand the distilled recipe of those calls is replayed by every later run with NO model in the loop.\n\nNEW MODULES (api/src/automation/)\n  discovery.ts             the goal loop. A SIBLING of runOrRehearse, not a reuse: rehearsal PATCHES a step list and its\n                           fixer may only local-patch the current index; discovery has no list and AUTHORS a recipe.\n                           It composes BrowserSession, the vision resolver, the fixer (for one failed act) and\n                           SecretRegistry, and adds the goal loop + the DISCOVERY_BUDGET re-plan/step/wall-clock caps.\n  discovery-goal-verify.ts the RUN-level gate. One EXPERT verify against the goal PLUS the captured evidence (call count\n                           and the value-free SHAPE of the last answer). Without it a pass compiles a recipe off a\n                           login wall. Reused verbatim by the heal.\n  network-capture.ts       the hosted redaction boundary + the model-free learner: redactCaptures -> internalApiCalls\n                           -> compileInjectedCalls / deriveLessons. Compiling needs no LLM, which is WHY run 2 is free.\n  response-shape.ts        expectShape: kinds and key names, never values. Drift = a key that DISAPPEARED, never one added.\n  executors/injected-call.ts  the replay ladder: in-page fetch -> node HTTP (PERMISSIVE origins only) -> scripted DOM.\n                           Vision is NOT a rung - it is the caller's fall-through, so a replay cannot silently cost tokens.\n  replay-action.ts         the MOUNT. Reads the recipe through recipe-store (ORG-SCOPED) - never through the definition\n                           projection, which strips recipes so they cannot reach the wire.\n  discovery-service.ts     the phase entry: run a pass, write evidence, then the recipe that points at it.\n  self-heal.ts             drift -> re-discover -> supersedeRecipe (tenant-scoped, version bumped, lineage stamped).\n                           NEVER publishSnapshot: its gate is super-admin AND it flips the row to global.\n\nWHERE IT MOUNTS. automation/service.ts runAutomationForAction tries the recipe BEFORE running the automation. Every\noutcome except ok and write-gate falls THROUGH to the old path, so the worst case is the run as it was before P2.\nwrite-gate does not fall through - a non-idempotent replay stops for a human (trap T4) and routing around it would\nmake the gate decorative. action-executor.ts passes integrationKey/actionName additively for that lookup.\n\nTHE MACHINE HALF (clients/bridge/src/browser/). capture.ts records request/response pairs, keeps header NAMES, and\nholds the live header VALUES in memory for the lease so inject.ts can forward them into an in-page fetch. Values never\ncross the wire in either direction: the LocalBrowserCapture / LocalBrowserInjectedCall schemas have no field for one.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
