   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (f) - P2 ROUND SIX: a replay is INDISTINGUISHABLE from the run it replaces.\n\nSame envelope, same answer, same failure modes - and nothing else changes. Five defects, one rule.\n\nONE ENVELOPE (api/src/automation/service.ts)\n  ActionRunEnvelope {runId, status, summary?, output, replayed?, recipeVersion?} + actionRunEnvelope(),\n  used by BOTH legs of runAutomationForAction. The replay leg used to answer a second shape\n  ({replayed, recipeVersion, output}) and every consumer reads the first: user-defined-poll.ts\n  unwraps `output` only for an envelope carrying a string runId AND a string status, so a REPLAYED\n  poll resolved its listenerConfig paths against the envelope, read undefined, and reported a quiet\n  provider forever (nothing clears a recipe that keeps succeeding).\n  The replay's runId is the `replay-<uuid>` its browser lease and its daemon frames are ledgered\n  under - minted in runAutomationForAction and threaded through ReplayActionInput.runId - so it\n  names a real execution. The prefix is what says no automationRuns document exists behind it.\n\nTHE ANSWER IS CORRELATED, NOT GUESSED\n  IntegrationActionRecipe gains `answersWith {callIndex, matchedBy:'run-output-identity'}` (STORED\n  SHAPE, additive; range-checked in parseCompiledRecipe and refused by recipe-store's cloneDraft if\n  it does not index a call beside it). compileInjectedCalls now REQUIRES `runOutput` - what the\n  learning run itself answered - and decides three ways:\n    the run answered nothing        -> no pointer; the replay answers nothing too. Every browser-only\n                                       automation this repo ships is this case (StepOutput exists for\n                                       api_call/ekoa_action/local_command only).\n    the answer IS a captured body   -> that call, matched by identity over canonical JSON.\n    the answer is none of them      -> REFUSE TO LEARN. A recipe that cannot reproduce the answer can\n                                       only answer with some other call's body, under success:true.\n  replayCompiledAction reads the pointer instead of calls[calls.length-1] - which was the order the\n  page's own responses COMPLETED in, so one badge poll after a search changed the action's answer.\n\nA NEW REPLAY OUTCOME (executors/injected-call.ts)\n  `arguments-uncovered` - there IS a readable recipe and it has no hole for an argument this caller\n  passes. Split out of `no-recipe` because the DISPOSITION differs: the caller CLEARS the recipe, as\n  it does for write-gate and does-not-cover. Without that the listener shape ({} on the establishing\n  tick, {since} on every tick after) left the narrow recipe in the action's only slot for the life of\n  the row. A NON-SCALAR argument stays `no-recipe`: no recipe could carry it, so dropping the stored\n  one would cost the optimisation over a caller's mistake. classifyReplayDrift calls it `refused`.\n\nTHREE BOUNDS ON THE HOSTED CAPTURE PATH (the machine has bounded itself all along)\n  browser-session.ts MAX_SESSION_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400, oldest dropped - the mirror of the\n    machine's per-lease MAX_BUFFERED_EXCHANGES, restated rather than imported (api/ may not import\n    clients/). This side accumulates ACROSS FRAMES until something drains it.\n  service.ts MAX_RUN_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400 across the run's frames, same discipline.\n  service.ts persistEvidence writes only internalApiCalls - the exact set a recipe can be distilled\n    from - bounded at MAX_PERSISTED_EVIDENCE = 2 x MAX_COMPILED_CALLS. It used to write one Mongo\n    document per captured request, in the API process every tenant shares.\n\nTHE BINDING IS TESTED (tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts, NEW)\n  server.ts's one line - `automationBackedActionHandler()` - was a surviving mutant: the pre-P2\n  inline mapping type-checks, drops the action identity and the write assent, and left the whole lane\n  green with the slice dead. The suite boots the REAL buildApp with the seams reset and enters at the\n  bound executeIntegrationAction. No module moved and no seam was added for it.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (f) - P2 ROUND SIX: a replay is INDISTINGUISHABLE from the run it replaces.\n\nSame envelope, same answer, same failure modes - and nothing else changes. Five defects, one rule.\n\nONE ENVELOPE (api/src/automation/service.ts)\n  ActionRunEnvelope {runId, status, summary?, output, replayed?, recipeVersion?} + actionRunEnvelope(),\n  used by BOTH legs of runAutomationForAction. The replay leg used to answer a second shape\n  ({replayed, recipeVersion, output}) and every consumer reads the first: user-defined-poll.ts\n  unwraps `output` only for an envelope carrying a string runId AND a string status, so a REPLAYED\n  poll resolved its listenerConfig paths against the envelope, read undefined, and reported a quiet\n  provider forever (nothing clears a recipe that keeps succeeding).\n  The replay's runId is the `replay-<uuid>` its browser lease and its daemon frames are ledgered\n  under - minted in runAutomationForAction and threaded through ReplayActionInput.runId - so it\n  names a real execution. The prefix is what says no automationRuns document exists behind it.\n\nTHE ANSWER IS CORRELATED, NOT GUESSED\n  IntegrationActionRecipe gains `answersWith {callIndex, matchedBy:'run-output-identity'}` (STORED\n  SHAPE, additive; range-checked in parseCompiledRecipe and refused by recipe-store's cloneDraft if\n  it does not index a call beside it). compileInjectedCalls now REQUIRES `runOutput` - what the\n  learning run itself answered - and decides three ways:\n    the run answered nothing        -> no pointer; the replay answers nothing too. Every browser-only\n                                       automation this repo ships is this case (StepOutput exists for\n                                       api_call/ekoa_action/local_command only).\n    the answer IS a captured body   -> that call, matched by identity over canonical JSON.\n    the answer is none of them      -> REFUSE TO LEARN. A recipe that cannot reproduce the answer can\n                                       only answer with some other call's body, under success:true.\n  replayCompiledAction reads the pointer instead of calls[calls.length-1] - which was the order the\n  page's own responses COMPLETED in, so one badge poll after a search changed the action's answer.\n\nA NEW REPLAY OUTCOME (executors/injected-call.ts)\n  `arguments-uncovered` - there IS a readable recipe and it has no hole for an argument this caller\n  passes. Split out of `no-recipe` because the DISPOSITION differs: the caller CLEARS the recipe, as\n  it does for write-gate and does-not-cover. Without that the listener shape ({} on the establishing\n  tick, {since} on every tick after) left the narrow recipe in the action's only slot for the life of\n  the row. A NON-SCALAR argument stays `no-recipe`: no recipe could carry it, so dropping the stored\n  one would cost the optimisation over a caller's mistake. classifyReplayDrift calls it `refused`.\n\nTHREE BOUNDS ON THE HOSTED CAPTURE PATH (the machine has bounded itself all along)\n  browser-session.ts MAX_SESSION_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400, oldest dropped - the mirror of the\n    machine's per-lease MAX_BUFFERED_EXCHANGES, restated rather than imported (api/ may not import\n    clients/). This side accumulates ACROSS FRAMES until something drains it.\n  service.ts MAX_RUN_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400 across the run's frames, same discipline.\n  service.ts persistEvidence writes only internalApiCalls - the exact set a recipe can be distilled\n    from - bounded at MAX_PERSISTED_EVIDENCE = 2 x MAX_COMPILED_CALLS. It used to write one Mongo\n    document per captured request, in the API process every tenant shares.\n\nTHE BINDING IS TESTED (tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts, NEW)\n  server.ts's one line - `automationBackedActionHandler()` - was a surviving mutant: the pre-P2\n  inline mapping type-checks, drops the action identity and the write assent, and left the whole lane\n  green with the slice dead. The suite boots the REAL buildApp with the seams reset and enters at the\n  bound executeIntegrationAction. No module moved and no seam was added for it.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (f) - P2 ROUND SIX: a replay is INDISTINGUISHABLE from the run it replaces.\n\nSame envelope, same answer, same failure modes - and nothing else changes. Five defects, one rule.\n\nONE ENVELOPE (api/src/automation/service.ts)\n  ActionRunEnvelope {runId, status, summary?, output, replayed?, recipeVersion?} + actionRunEnvelope(),\n  used by BOTH legs of runAutomationForAction. The replay leg used to answer a second shape\n  ({replayed, recipeVersion, output}) and every consumer reads the first: user-defined-poll.ts\n  unwraps `output` only for an envelope carrying a string runId AND a string status, so a REPLAYED\n  poll resolved its listenerConfig paths against the envelope, read undefined, and reported a quiet\n  provider forever (nothing clears a recipe that keeps succeeding).\n  The replay's runId is the `replay-<uuid>` its browser lease and its daemon frames are ledgered\n  under - minted in runAutomationForAction and threaded through ReplayActionInput.runId - so it\n  names a real execution. The prefix is what says no automationRuns document exists behind it.\n\nTHE ANSWER IS CORRELATED, NOT GUESSED\n  IntegrationActionRecipe gains `answersWith {callIndex, matchedBy:'run-output-identity'}` (STORED\n  SHAPE, additive; range-checked in parseCompiledRecipe and refused by recipe-store's cloneDraft if\n  it does not index a call beside it). compileInjectedCalls now REQUIRES `runOutput` - what the\n  learning run itself answered - and decides three ways:\n    the run answered nothing        -> no pointer; the replay answers nothing too. Every browser-only\n                                       automation this repo ships is this case (StepOutput exists for\n                                       api_call/ekoa_action/local_command only).\n    the answer IS a captured body   -> that call, matched by identity over canonical JSON.\n    the answer is none of them      -> REFUSE TO LEARN. A recipe that cannot reproduce the answer can\n                                       only answer with some other call's body, under success:true.\n  replayCompiledAction reads the pointer instead of calls[calls.length-1] - which was the order the\n  page's own responses COMPLETED in, so one badge poll after a search changed the action's answer.\n\nA NEW REPLAY OUTCOME (executors/injected-call.ts)\n  `arguments-uncovered` - there IS a readable recipe and it has no hole for an argument this caller\n  passes. Split out of `no-recipe` because the DISPOSITION differs: the caller CLEARS the recipe, as\n  it does for write-gate and does-not-cover. Without that the listener shape ({} on the establishing\n  tick, {since} on every tick after) left the narrow recipe in the action's only slot for the life of\n  the row. A NON-SCALAR argument stays `no-recipe`: no recipe could carry it, so dropping the stored\n  one would cost the optimisation over a caller's mistake. classifyReplayDrift calls it `refused`.\n\nTHREE BOUNDS ON THE HOSTED CAPTURE PATH (the machine has bounded itself all along)\n  browser-session.ts MAX_SESSION_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400, oldest dropped - the mirror of the\n    machine's per-lease MAX_BUFFERED_EXCHANGES, restated rather than imported (api/ may not import\n    clients/). This side accumulates ACROSS FRAMES until something drains it.\n  service.ts MAX_RUN_CAPTURED_EXCHANGES = 400 across the run's frames, same discipline.\n  service.ts persistEvidence writes only internalApiCalls - the exact set a recipe can be distilled\n    from - bounded at MAX_PERSISTED_EVIDENCE = 2 x MAX_COMPILED_CALLS. It used to write one Mongo\n    document per captured request, in the API process every tenant shares.\n\nTHE BINDING IS TESTED (tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts, NEW)\n  server.ts's one line - `automationBackedActionHandler()` - was a surviving mutant: the pre-P2\n  inline mapping type-checks, drops the action identity and the write assent, and left the whole lane\n  green with the slice dead. The suite boots the REAL buildApp with the seams reset and enters at the\n  bound executeIntegrationAction. No module moved and no seam was added for it.",
