   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): TWO new modules, one new seam across a\ntier boundary, and one call-site change that makes graduation mean something.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts (tier 3) - owns the integration_action_evidence\ncollection (see 05-data-model), its caps, and the LAST GATE: the whole assembled document is\nre-checked against the run's live SecretRegistry and a row carrying a live value is NOT WRITTEN.\nNo new redaction machinery exists in it - the api-call sample IS the executor's own requestSummary,\nthe object action-executor.ts already builds on every call through redactSecretsDeep and already\npersists verbatim on the FAILURE path. Reusing the failure path's redaction is the safety argument:\nif it were wrong here it would have been leaking the identical bytes since C2.\n\nNEW api/src/automation/action-evidence.ts (tier 4) - the automation half. It exists BECAUSE of\nFIXED-1: reading a run means reading RunRecord / StepRecord.output / the screenshot layout, all of\nwhich live in automation/, a tier integrations/ may not import. So action-executor.ts declares a\n`RunEvidenceCollector` seam and server.ts binds it, exactly as it already binds\nrunAutomationBackedAction. The two halves meet at the composition root and nowhere else.\n\nTHE SEAM BUNDLE. ExecutorDeps gains recordActionEvidence + collectRunEvidence, and server.ts binds\nthem ONCE into a single `executorDeps` object that all four executor call sites now spread. The\nbundling is the point: that file's own comment already warned a call site omitting\nrunAutomationBackedAction 'silently breaks every automation-backed action', and a second seam with\nthe same failure mode would double the chance of a half-landed wiring. A bundle threads whole.\n\nCAPTURE POINTS. api-call: on 2xx, where the requestSummary was previously DISCARDED (the failure\npath was the only thing that kept it). automation-backed: on success, reading runId off\nActionRunEnvelope and collecting POINTERS - never copies of the PNGs, which stay behind the\nauthenticated screenshot plane that already enforces org + owner on every byte. Capture is\nbest-effort and loud: the action has already run, so a throw here must never turn a succeeded call\ninto a failed one (the discardEvidenceOfRemovedRecipes posture).\n\nRETENTION. sweepExpiredScreenshots gains a `pinnedRunIds` exemption so a run named by live evidence\nsurvives its own expiry. Bounded to the ONE run each action's live evidence names, and a superseding\nrun releases the previous pin in the same write. IT IS AN AGE-SWEEP EXEMPTION AND NOT AN ERASURE\nSTORY - there is no erasure path over this tree at all (finding\n`screenshot-erasure-path-has-no-production-caller`), so a pinned run is retained past 7 days with\nnothing able to remove it on request. Recorded as a gap, not papered over.\n\nGRADUATION GAINS TEETH. promoteToTrusted (authored-action.ts) previously proved SHAPE and never\nBEHAVIOUR: every guardrail is a property of the DRAFT, so an action could graduate to `trusted` -\nand so become auto-runnable by achieve - having NEVER RUN ONCE. It now takes a REQUIRED `evidence`\nargument positioned BEFORE the defaulted `now`, so a caller cannot forget it because omitting it\ndoes not compile, and refuses `unvalidated` when it is absent, when its `shape` names different\nbytes, or when it carries no shape at all. Its ONE production caller (integration-achieve.ts\ntrustAuthoredAction, the single line slice S1 changes in that file) supplies the row; mutating that\nline to `null` reddens 4 cases, which is what stops the gate being the dead-binding class this repo\nhas now produced four times.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): TWO new modules, one new seam across a\ntier boundary, and one call-site change that makes graduation mean something.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts (tier 3) - owns the integration_action_evidence\ncollection (see 05-data-model), its caps, and the LAST GATE: the whole assembled document is\nre-checked against the run's live SecretRegistry and a row carrying a live value is NOT WRITTEN.\nNo new redaction machinery exists in it - the api-call sample IS the executor's own requestSummary,\nthe object action-executor.ts already builds on every call through redactSecretsDeep and already\npersists verbatim on the FAILURE path. Reusing the failure path's redaction is the safety argument:\nif it were wrong here it would have been leaking the identical bytes since C2.\n\nNEW api/src/automation/action-evidence.ts (tier 4) - the automation half. It exists BECAUSE of\nFIXED-1: reading a run means reading RunRecord / StepRecord.output / the screenshot layout, all of\nwhich live in automation/, a tier integrations/ may not import. So action-executor.ts declares a\n`RunEvidenceCollector` seam and server.ts binds it, exactly as it already binds\nrunAutomationBackedAction. The two halves meet at the composition root and nowhere else.\n\nTHE SEAM BUNDLE. ExecutorDeps gains recordActionEvidence + collectRunEvidence, and server.ts binds\nthem ONCE into a single `executorDeps` object that all four executor call sites now spread. The\nbundling is the point: that file's own comment already warned a call site omitting\nrunAutomationBackedAction 'silently breaks every automation-backed action', and a second seam with\nthe same failure mode would double the chance of a half-landed wiring. A bundle threads whole.\n\nCAPTURE POINTS. api-call: on 2xx, where the requestSummary was previously DISCARDED (the failure\npath was the only thing that kept it). automation-backed: on success, reading runId off\nActionRunEnvelope and collecting POINTERS - never copies of the PNGs, which stay behind the\nauthenticated screenshot plane that already enforces org + owner on every byte. Capture is\nbest-effort and loud: the action has already run, so a throw here must never turn a succeeded call\ninto a failed one (the discardEvidenceOfRemovedRecipes posture).\n\nRETENTION. sweepExpiredScreenshots gains a `pinnedRunIds` exemption so a run named by live evidence\nsurvives its own expiry. Bounded to the ONE run each action's live evidence names, and a superseding\nrun releases the previous pin in the same write. IT IS AN AGE-SWEEP EXEMPTION AND NOT AN ERASURE\nSTORY - there is no erasure path over this tree at all (finding\n`screenshot-erasure-path-has-no-production-caller`), so a pinned run is retained past 7 days with\nnothing able to remove it on request. Recorded as a gap, not papered over.\n\nGRADUATION GAINS TEETH. promoteToTrusted (authored-action.ts) previously proved SHAPE and never\nBEHAVIOUR: every guardrail is a property of the DRAFT, so an action could graduate to `trusted` -\nand so become auto-runnable by achieve - having NEVER RUN ONCE. It now takes a REQUIRED `evidence`\nargument positioned BEFORE the defaulted `now`, so a caller cannot forget it because omitting it\ndoes not compile, and refuses `unvalidated` when it is absent, when its `shape` names different\nbytes, or when it carries no shape at all. Its ONE production caller (integration-achieve.ts\ntrustAuthoredAction, the single line slice S1 changes in that file) supplies the row; mutating that\nline to `null` reddens 4 cases, which is what stops the gate being the dead-binding class this repo\nhas now produced four times.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): TWO new modules, one new seam across a\ntier boundary, and one call-site change that makes graduation mean something.\n\nNEW api/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts (tier 3) - owns the integration_action_evidence\ncollection (see 05-data-model), its caps, and the LAST GATE: the whole assembled document is\nre-checked against the run's live SecretRegistry and a row carrying a live value is NOT WRITTEN.\nNo new redaction machinery exists in it - the api-call sample IS the executor's own requestSummary,\nthe object action-executor.ts already builds on every call through redactSecretsDeep and already\npersists verbatim on the FAILURE path. Reusing the failure path's redaction is the safety argument:\nif it were wrong here it would have been leaking the identical bytes since C2.\n\nNEW api/src/automation/action-evidence.ts (tier 4) - the automation half. It exists BECAUSE of\nFIXED-1: reading a run means reading RunRecord / StepRecord.output / the screenshot layout, all of\nwhich live in automation/, a tier integrations/ may not import. So action-executor.ts declares a\n`RunEvidenceCollector` seam and server.ts binds it, exactly as it already binds\nrunAutomationBackedAction. The two halves meet at the composition root and nowhere else.\n\nTHE SEAM BUNDLE. ExecutorDeps gains recordActionEvidence + collectRunEvidence, and server.ts binds\nthem ONCE into a single `executorDeps` object that all four executor call sites now spread. The\nbundling is the point: that file's own comment already warned a call site omitting\nrunAutomationBackedAction 'silently breaks every automation-backed action', and a second seam with\nthe same failure mode would double the chance of a half-landed wiring. A bundle threads whole.\n\nCAPTURE POINTS. api-call: on 2xx, where the requestSummary was previously DISCARDED (the failure\npath was the only thing that kept it). automation-backed: on success, reading runId off\nActionRunEnvelope and collecting POINTERS - never copies of the PNGs, which stay behind the\nauthenticated screenshot plane that already enforces org + owner on every byte. Capture is\nbest-effort and loud: the action has already run, so a throw here must never turn a succeeded call\ninto a failed one (the discardEvidenceOfRemovedRecipes posture).\n\nRETENTION. sweepExpiredScreenshots gains a `pinnedRunIds` exemption so a run named by live evidence\nsurvives its own expiry. Bounded to the ONE run each action's live evidence names, and a superseding\nrun releases the previous pin in the same write. IT IS AN AGE-SWEEP EXEMPTION AND NOT AN ERASURE\nSTORY - there is no erasure path over this tree at all (finding\n`screenshot-erasure-path-has-no-production-caller`), so a pinned run is retained past 7 days with\nnothing able to remove it on request. Recorded as a gap, not papered over.\n\nGRADUATION GAINS TEETH. promoteToTrusted (authored-action.ts) previously proved SHAPE and never\nBEHAVIOUR: every guardrail is a property of the DRAFT, so an action could graduate to `trusted` -\nand so become auto-runnable by achieve - having NEVER RUN ONCE. It now takes a REQUIRED `evidence`\nargument positioned BEFORE the defaulted `now`, so a caller cannot forget it because omitting it\ndoes not compile, and refuses `unvalidated` when it is absent, when its `shape` names different\nbytes, or when it carries no shape at all. Its ONE production caller (integration-achieve.ts\ntrustAuthoredAction, the single line slice S1 changes in that file) supplies the row; mutating that\nline to `null` reddens 4 cases, which is what stops the gate being the dead-binding class this repo\nhas now produced four times."
  }
 ]
}
